From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:16:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gateway): a graceful restart hands each running turn
 over at its own step boundary

gateway.restart_turn_handoff_per_turn (false = off) and restart_turn_carry_ceiling_seconds (1080), with
restart_turn_handoff_boundary. The restarting gateway releases the profile at once and carries only its
running turns: each is handed off at its own step boundary and resumed by the next gateway within a poll,
or settles where it ends. The next gateway leaves the carrier's claims alone while its lock is held,
relays its event frames to its own viewers and forwards Stop, steer and prompt answers to it. New API
requests on the carrier are forwarded to the next gateway; its open runs finish where they are. A step
past restart_turn_handoff_wait_seconds is not stopped; only the ceiling stops a turn the 0048 way.
